reference:
Image processing (low-level) focuses on enhancement/noise removal;
analysis (mid-level) focuses on segmentation; vision (high-level) focuses on
emulation of human sight and object recognition.

Unsharp Masking: The process involves three steps: ( 1 ) blurring the original
image, ( 2) subtracting the blurred image from the original to create a mask, and (3
) adding the mask back to the original to produce a sharper image.
